    "description": "DataBank provides colocation, interconnection, and managed infrastructure services for enterprise, cloud, and artificial-intelligence workloads. Its customers include enterprises, hyperscale users, and network counterparties that require data-center capacity, connectivity, and related managed services across multiple U.S. markets. The operating model is asset-heavy because the business owns and operates data-center facilities and critical power and cooling infrastructure, with revenues generated through long-term capacity, colocation, and service contracts. AustralianSuper describes the platform as one of the larger North American data-center operators, and public disclosures in 2024 referenced more than 65 data centers across 27 key markets and a build-out plan exceeding 850 MW of additional capacity. DataBank was founded in 2005, DigitalBridge has been a long-term sponsor since 2016, and AustralianSuper became a significant minority owner through the 2024 equity raise.",
